"""Build a self-contained, offline-readable research report from verified outputs."""
from pathlib import Path
import json,base64,html
import pandas as pd

def build_report(out):
 out=Path(out);s=json.loads((out/'summary.json').read_text());m=s['modelling'];v=s['survival'];b=s['biology']
 def table(df):return df.to_html(index=False,border=0,float_format=lambda x:f'{x:.4g}',escape=True,classes='data')
 def fig(name,caption):
  p=out/name
  if not p.exists():return ''
  data=base64.b64encode(p.read_bytes()).decode();return f'<figure><img src="data:image/png;base64,{data}" alt="{html.escape(caption)}"><figcaption>{html.escape(caption)}</figcaption></figure>'
 cv=pd.read_csv(out/'nested_cv_fold_metrics.csv').groupby('model')[['roc_auc','balanced_accuracy','macro_f1']].mean().reset_index().sort_values('roc_auc',ascending=False)
 paths=pd.read_csv(out/'pathway_hypoxia_associations.csv').sort_values('fdr');top=pd.read_csv(out/'selected_predictive_genes.csv').head(15)
 hr=v['cox_hypoxia_HR_per_SD'];lo,hi=v['cox_hypoxia_HR_CI95'];auc=m['holdout']['roc_auc'];ci=m['holdout']['auc_bootstrap_95CI'];ph=v['PH_hypoxia_p']
 text=f'''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>TCGA LUAD Hypoxia Research Results</title><style>
 body{{font:16px/1.65 system-ui,Arial,sans-serif;color:#243442;background:#f3f5f7;margin:0}}main{{max-width:1050px;margin:auto;padding:40px 35px;background:white}}h1{{font-size:34px;line-height:1.15}}h2{{margin-top:38px;color:#173e57}}.status{{background:#fff4db;padding:16px;border-radius:8px}}.metrics{{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:18px}}.metric{{padding:15px;background:#eef4f7;flex:1;min-width:170px}}.metric strong{{display:block;font-size:27px}}table{{border-collapse:collapse;font-size:14px;width:100%;overflow-wrap:anywhere}}td,th{{padding:8px 10px;border:1px solid #dce2e8;text-align:left}}th{{background:#eaf0f5}}img{{max-width:100%;height:auto}}figure{{margin:20px 0}}figcaption{{color:#536575;font-size:14px}}.grid{{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(350px,1fr));gap:25px}}a{{color:#165d86}}code{{background:#eef1f3;padding:2px 4px}}footer{{margin-top:35px;font-size:13px;color:#5b6a75}}@media print{{body{{background:white}}main{{padding:0}}h2{{break-after:avoid}}figure{{break-inside:avoid}}}}</style><main>
 <p>RESEARCH ANALYSIS · TCGA-LUAD · fixed seed {s['seed']}</p><h1>Tumor hypoxia and metabolic gene expression</h1>
 <p>We calculated a gene-expression-based hypoxia score for each selected primary tumor, explored metabolic associations, compared six prediction models and analyzed overall survival.</p>
 <p class="status"><strong>What the model predicts:</strong> an RNA-derived high/low hypoxia group, not measured oxygen, treatment response or an individual clinical outcome. Independent patient-cohort validation has <strong>not</strong> been performed.</p>
 <div class="metrics"><div class="metric"><strong>{s['cohort']}</strong>unique patients</div><div class="metric"><strong>{auc:.3f}</strong>untouched-test ROC AUC</div><div class="metric"><strong>{m['test_extremes_evaluated']}</strong>test patients with extreme labels</div><div class="metric"><strong>{v['survival_n']}</strong>valid survival records</div></div>
 <h2>1. Data and hypoxia scoring</h2><p>The public Xena TPM matrix was downloaded directly and its metadata verified as log₂(TPM + 1). We selected the lexicographically first primary tumor sample per patient, averaged duplicate-symbol log-expression rows, and retained a broad fixed background for scoring. All original data and exclusions are audited in the CSV and JSON outputs.</p>
 <p>Hallmark Hypoxia contains 200 symbols; 199 matched directly and HACL2 was omitted without an unverified alias substitution. GSEApy ssGSEA used within-sample ranks and exponent 0.25. We use raw <strong>ES</strong>, not the cohort-rescaled NES, so another patient's presence does not change a patient's score. A single-sample invariance check passed.</p>
 <p>Descriptive tertile groups: {html.escape(str(s['groups']))}. For prediction, cutoffs are learned within training data and frozen before application to test patients.</p>{fig('hypoxia_distribution.png','Raw hypoxia enrichment score distribution; dashed lines show full-cohort descriptive tertiles.')}
 <h2>2. Exploration and clustering</h2><p>PCA, ICA, t-SNE and UMAP are exploratory views of variable genes outside the hypoxia-scoring set. They are not model validation. Clustering uses 20 PCA components; the two plotted axes are only a visualization. K was selected using silhouette score rather than agreement with the hypoxia labels.</p>
 <div class="grid">{fig('pca.png','PCA, colored afterward by the calculated hypoxia group.')}{fig('umap.png','UMAP, colored afterward by the calculated hypoxia group.')}{fig('pca_scree.png','Cumulative variance explained by principal components.')}{fig('cluster_counts.png','Counts of existing hypoxia labels inside the selected K-Means clusters.')}</div>
 <p>Additional outputs include ICA and t-SNE plots, clustering metrics for K=2–8, hierarchical clustering and DBSCAN, seed stability, and example distribution/QQ checks.</p>
 <h2>3. Gene and metabolic pathway associations</h2><p>We tested {b['genes_tested']:,} adequately expressed genes using Welch tests with Benjamini–Hochberg correction; Mann–Whitney tests provide a sensitivity comparison. A descriptive threshold of adjusted p &lt; 0.05 and absolute difference in mean log₂(TPM + 1) ≥ 0.5 identified {b['differing_genes_outside_signature']:,} differing genes outside the scoring set, including {b['differing_metabolic_genes']:,} genes in the chosen metabolic reference sets.</p>
 <p>These are descriptive full-cohort associations. Hypoxia is itself defined from the same expression experiment, so differences do not establish oxygen causation or metabolic flux. ORA removes hypoxia genes from its tested background. Metabolic ssGSEA scores below also omit hypoxia genes, reducing direct gene overlap.</p>{table(paths[['pathway','spearman_rho','fdr','matched_genes_without_hypoxia']])}
 <div class="grid">{fig('volcano.png','Differential-expression overview. The horizontal line marks adjusted p=0.05.')}{fig('pathway_correlations.png','Association between hypoxia and metabolic expression scores after removing overlapping scoring genes.')}</div>{fig('gene_heatmap.png','Top differing metabolic genes, standardized only for display; tumors ordered by hypoxia score.')}
 <h2>4. Prediction on unseen patients</h2><p>We reserved {m['test_patients_reserved']} patients before predictive fitting. The remaining {m['development_patients']} patients formed the development cohort. Six classifiers were compared using five outer development folds and three-fold inner tuning. All gene filtering, scaling and supervised feature selection were fitted within training folds. Predictors were drawn only from the nine prespecified metabolic/related gene sets, excluding every hypoxia-scoring gene.</p>
 <p><strong>Selected model: {html.escape(m['selected_model'])}.</strong> It was selected using development CV only, then fitted on {m['development_extremes_used']} development patients. Its frozen training-derived cutoffs were applied to the untouched test cohort; intermediate test patients were excluded according to this predeclared extreme-group task.</p>{table(cv)}
 <p>Final test AUC: <strong>{auc:.3f}</strong>, with a patient-bootstrap 95% interval of <strong>{ci[0]:.3f}–{ci[1]:.3f}</strong>. Balanced accuracy: {m['holdout']['balanced_accuracy']:.3f}; macro F1: {m['holdout']['macro_f1']:.3f}. This interval reflects finite test patients, not all training uncertainty. A dummy baseline AUC is {m['holdout']['dummy']['roc_auc']:.3f}; a clinical-only baseline using age, sex, stage and smoking exposure has AUC {m['holdout']['clinical_only_baseline']['roc_auc']:.3f}.</p>
 <div class="grid">{fig('holdout_roc.png','Final test ROC for the development-selected model.')}{fig('holdout_confusion.png','Final test prediction errors at probability threshold 0.5.')}</div>{fig('model_comparison.png','Mean outer development-fold AUC; bars show fold standard deviations.')}
 <p>The final pipeline retained {m['selected_genes']} genes. Weights/importances are model-specific and are not causal biomarker evidence.</p>{table(top)}
 <h2>5. Overall survival</h2><p>Survival event coding and time units were checked against clinical vital status and follow-up/death days. The analysis includes {v['survival_n']} patients with positive follow-up and {v['death_events']} deaths. The three-group log-rank p-value is <strong>{v['logrank_p']:.4g}</strong>.</p>
 <p>The exploratory Cox model used {v['cox_complete_case_n']} complete cases, adjusting for age, sex and categorical stage, with a small regularization penalty (0.01). Hypoxia hazard ratio per one score standard deviation: <strong>{hr:.3f}</strong> (95% CI {lo:.3f}–{hi:.3f}; p={v['cox_hypoxia_p']:.4g}). A hazard ratio above 1 indicates higher estimated hazard under the fitted model; it is not a patient-specific survival prediction.</p>
 <p>Proportional-hazards check for hypoxia: p={ph:.4g}. {'This flags a possible proportional-hazards violation; interpret the single hazard ratio with caution.' if ph<.05 else 'This check did not flag a hypoxia-specific violation at p<0.05; inspect all covariates and diagnostics in the CSV outputs.'} Missingness and clinical/treatment confounding remain limitations.</p><div class="grid">{fig('survival_km.png','Descriptive Kaplan–Meier curves for calculated hypoxia groups.')}{fig('cox_effects.png','Adjusted Cox associations with confidence intervals.')}</div>
 <p><strong>Survival sensitivity check:</strong> age/sex/stage-adjusted model diagnostics flagged sex and stage III proportional-hazards assumptions. A stage-and-sex-stratified Cox sensitivity analysis is supplied in the CSV outputs; interpret the simple hazard ratio as exploratory.</p><h2>6. What is complete and what remains</h2><ul><li>Complete: data audit, scores and groups, exploratory plots, clustering, gene/pathway comparisons, nested model comparison, untouched holdout evaluation, trained model export and survival analysis.</li><li>Pending: independent LUAD validation, experimental hypoxia validation and biological/clinical review. No external-cohort performance is claimed.</li><li>Test the frozen pipeline on a compatible independent RNA-seq cohort using <code>external_validate.py</code>. Strict gene-background and scale checks prevent silently incomparable scores.</li><li>These are research results. The labels are expression-derived proxies, and selecting extreme groups makes classification easier than the full continuous spectrum.</li></ul>
 <h2>Reproduce and inspect</h2><p>Run <code>python download_data.py</code> then <code>python pipeline.py</code> after installing the pinned requirements. The large public TPM matrix is intentionally downloaded rather than duplicated inside the ZIP. The archive includes all scripts, reference gene sets, clinical data, audit tables, plots, frozen model and results.</p>
 <p>Sources: <a href="https://xenabrowser.net/datapages/">UCSC Xena</a>; <a href="https://www.gsea-msigdb.org/gsea/msigdb/cards/HALLMARK_HYPOXIA">Hallmark Hypoxia</a>; <a href="https://www.gsea-msigdb.org/gsea/msigdb/collections.jsp">MSigDB Hallmarks</a>; <a href="https://gseapy.readthedocs.io/en/latest/">GSEApy documentation</a>; <a href="https://lifelines.readthedocs.io/">lifelines documentation</a>. Exact URLs, checksums and software versions are included in provenance files.</p>
 <footer>Generated from pipeline outputs. Seed {s['seed']}. This report contains computed results, not illustrative example numbers.</footer></main></html>'''
 (out/'report.html').write_text(text)
